Package: prism
Title: FIML Covariance Projection for Structural Equation Models with Missing Data
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: person("Xiyuan", "Guo", email = "tommyguo039@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Fits structural equation models (latent growth models, CFAs,
    and general SEMs) via FIML, extracts the model-implied covariance
    matrix, and projects an initial imputation onto that structural target
    under a regularized constrained objective that balances fidelity to the initial
    imputation against covariance matching while preserving column means.
    Supports single imputation (prism_fiml, prism_sem) and two-level proper
    multiple imputation (prism_mi) with stochastic initializations and
    parameter draws.
